      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Rapidly generated ai content needs to not only be tagged, but controlled to prevent unmanageable server stress and instability of the game connection. We thought user generated content was a lot? Its likely ai usage would more than triple the volume of uploaded content if left unchecked. It would be a noticeablly expensive impact, given the operating margins vrchat is at. For what? To what end does it make the concept of a virtual world for people to experience any better? Or does it only cause even worse obscuration and discoverability problems for great works?",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
